        "description": "Mid-cruise refinement."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 3,
        "type": "tcm",
        "label": "MCC-4",
        "description": "Mid-cruise refinement."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 3.27,
        "type": "tcm",
        "label": "MCC-5 — final pre-LOI",
        "description": "Final approach targeting."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 5,
        "type": "loi",
        "label": "Lunar orbit insertion",
        "description": "2020-11-28. Captured into 200-km circular lunar orbit.",
        "dv_km_s": 0.8
      },
      {
        "met_days": 8,
        "type": "descent_start",
        "label": "Powered descent — Mons Rümker",
        "description": "2020-12-01. Lander descended to Mons Rümker (43.06°N, 51.92°W) in Oceanus Procellarum — one of the youngest large lava-flow regions on the Moon. Drilled to ~1 m + scooped surface regolith, collecting 1,731 g."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 10,
        "type": "ascent",
        "label": "Ascent + lunar rendezvous",
        "description": "2020-12-03. Ascender lifted off the surface, rendezvoused + docked with the orbiter — China's first robotic rendezvous + docking around another body."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 19,
        "type": "tei",
        "label": "Trans-Earth injection",
        "description": "2020-12-12. Orbiter departed lunar orbit on return trajectory.",
        "dv_km_s": 0.9
      },
      {
        "met_days": 23,
        "type": "earth_return",
        "label": "Sample return capsule landing — Inner Mongolia",
        "description": "2020-12-16 (17:59 UTC). Capsule re-entered Earth's atmosphere using a skip-entry maneuver, parachuted to a soft landing in Inner Mongolia. Samples are some of the youngest lunar volcanic rocks (~1.97 Gyr) ever returned — extending the known Moon volcanism timeline."
      }
    ],
